From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:37:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 47/60] hjviewer: Android 7.0 (API 24) and later

Google Play's automatic protection, which the Play Console applies to the
app's bundles, needs a minimum SDK of 24: the Console refused the 1.6.0
bundle (minSdkVersion 22, Android 5.1). The app now runs on Android 7.0
and later; the side-loaded APK gets the same minimum. In-app updates
already needed Android 7.0, so every supported device now has them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/android/app/build.gradle | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/flutter/android/app/build.gradle b/flutter/android/app/build.gradle
index 2817853..5427095 100644
--- a/flutter/android/app/build.gradle
+++ b/flutter/android/app/build.gradle
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ android {
     defaultConfig {
         // TODO: Specify your own unique Application ID (https://developer.android.com/studio/build/application-id.html).
         applicationId "kr.ac.yonsei.hjviewer"
-        minSdkVersion 22
+        minSdkVersion 24
         targetSdkVersion 36
         versionCode flutterVersionCode.toInteger()
         versionName flutterVersionName
